From: Construct <release@constructlinux.org>
Subject: gdesktopappinfo: Keep an app's earliest match when it matches a token more than once

When an app matches a search token several times with the same match
type and category - "se" in more than one of Firefox's keywords -
merge_token_results() keeps the entry compare_results() sorts first,
and compare_results() did not order those entries: qsort() is not
stable, so which token position survived changed from one search to the
next. g_desktop_app_info_search() groups results by token position too,
so the app moved between groups: GNOME Shell's search showed Firefox
before Google Chrome in one session and after it in the next.

Order an app's entries by token position as well, so its earliest match
is the one kept, as compare_categories() already prefers.

--- a/gio/gdesktopappinfo.c
+++ b/gio/gdesktopappinfo.c
@@ -574,7 +574,13 @@ compare_results (gconstpointer a,
       if (ra->match_type != rb->match_type)
         return ra->match_type - rb->match_type;
 
-      return ra->category - rb->category;
+      if (ra->category != rb->category)
+        return ra->category - rb->category;
+
+      /* The earliest match of the best kind is the one kept: qsort() is not
+       * stable, and which of several left first changed between searches.
+       */
+      return ra->token_pos - rb->token_pos;
     }
 }
 
